Maria (she/her): Hey team — can someone take a quick look at a small docs PR? Adds a concise JS quickstart snippet and clarifies auth header differences between hosted vs private deployments. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/421. Hoping to merge before 10:00am PT tomorrow for a demo. cc @Shyam @Kevin

Shyam: On it. Quick question — does the example show `Authorization: Bearer <API_KEY>` or use an `x-api-key` header for private installs? Customers keep confusing these in support tickets.

Maria (she/her): Good call — for hosted we use `Authorization: Bearer <API_KEY>`; for Private we recommend an `x-api-key` example and call out KMS handling in the note. Tiny snippet from the PR: ```js
// quickstart: send a prompt
const res = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ model: 'rwd-medium', input: 'Hello' })
});
const json = await res.json();
console.log(json.output);
```

Docs Bot: docs-ci / lint: passed ✅ (link-checks ok)

Kevin: I can review now, ping me if I disappear. Skimming — nits around wording of "customer-managed key" and one env var name. Also add a tiny note about token rotation.

Maria (she/her): thanks — updated wording to "customer-managed KMS (KMS/HSM)" and added a one-line note about rotation. pushed a follow-up commit.

Shyam: LGTM from me. One tiny nit: add a blank line after the fenced code block for readability.

Olivia: quick ops note — standard merge window for docs is 9:00–11:00am PT. If you need this in prod for tomorrow's demo, target merge by 9:30 so the CDN refresh completes.

Kevin: reviewed + approved. Left an inline comment suggesting `REDWOOD_API_KEY` -> `REDWOOD_API_KEY` (nit: we prefer uppercase all-caps env var examples), but that can be fixed separately. :+1:

Maria (she/her): Awesome — thanks everyone. I'll merge after a final CI rerun (Docs Bot already green). If anything weird appears post-merge I'll revert and ping the channel. :thumbsup:

